      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "I have a **keepable but not stellar** hand. Here's the breakdown:\n\n- **Goblin Warchief**: Strong 2-drop for a Goblin deck, reduces costs and gives haste.\n- **Tectonic Giant**: Solid 4-drop with upside, but slow.\n- **Soul Read**: Flexible counter/draw spell, but expensive.\n- **Synchronized Eviction**: Conditional cost reduction, but situational.\n- **2x Island, Thriving Bluff**: Solid mana base, but I’m light on early plays.\n\n**Problems**:\n- No 1-drop or 3-drop, which is awkward for curve.\n- Only 2 lands (3 if I count Thriving Bluff, but it enters tapped).\n- Soul Read and Synchronized Eviction are expensive and situational.\n\n**Upside**:\n- Goblin Warchief is a great card for a Goblin deck.\n- Tectonic Giant is a strong finisher.\n- Thriving Bluff is a solid land.\n\n**Mulligan Decision**:\n- I’m on the play, so I can afford to be a little greedy.\n- The hand is **keepable**, but it’s **slow** and **light on early interaction**.\n- If I mulligan, I risk missing land drops or getting stuck with worse cards.\n\n**Verdict**: I’ll **keep** this hand. It’s not perfect, but it has a reasonable curve and strong payoffs. I’ll hope to draw a 1-drop or another land to smooth things out.",
